  "summary": {
    "ideas": [
      "`pre[i]` is the sum of the first `i` items, with `pre[0] = 0`. So `pre` has $n + 1$ entries and is built in one pass.",
      "Any range is two lookups: `sum(xs[i:j]) == pre[j] - pre[i]`, using the slice's own indices.",
      "Counting runs that sum to $k$ is a dict of prefix counts: each day adds `seen[pre - k]`, starting from `{0: 1}`."
    ],
    "formula": {
      "name": "Range sum",
      "tex": "\\sum_{t=i}^{j-1} x_t = P_j - P_i",
      "note": "With $P_0 = 0$ there is no special case at the start of the list."
    },
    "trap": "`pre[j] - pre[i - 1]` with $n$ entries reads `pre[-1]` when `i = 0`: Python wraps to the last entry, with no error."
  },
